Z||000007||FieroJoe||03-13-2001||07:47 AM||||Well It seems like it could be the fan temp switch.  I have rodney's low temp switch, Ill post a pic of it if I get a chance tonight to (at school right now)<P>My 84-86's are different than the DIS 2.5.  The only two temp sensors of any kind that I have on mine is the one in the blcok, that is whown in your pic, and the on on the stat neck.  If you dont have a sensor on your t-stat filler neck I would assume that your broken one is the fan switch.<P>Good Luck, and could this be your overheating problem?  Or did you get that worked out already?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
